===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sed-}}
From {{m|en|set|pos=verb}} + {{m|en|about|pos=adverb, preposition}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|subentry=to set about|subpos=phrasal v|subid=4802840598|entry=set|pos=''v.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=6993814720|date=September 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=phrasal v}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/sɛt‿əˈbaʊt/|a=RP,GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|aʊt|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|set<,,set> about}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Used with the {{glossary|adverb}} sense of ''about''.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|chiefly|Northern England}} To [[circulate]] or [[spread#Verb|spread]] ([[news#Noun|news]], a [[rumor#Noun|rumour]], etc.)
# {{non-gloss definition|Used with the {{glossary|preposition}} sense of ''about''.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}}
### {{lb|en|passive voice}} To [[encircle]] or [[surround#Verb|surround]] (something) with other [[thing]]s.
### {{lb|en|UK|informal}} To [[attack#Verb|attack]] (someone); to [[set upon]].
###: {{synonyms|en|begin upon}}
###: {{ux|en|Two youths '''set about''' him.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[start#Verb|start]] [[do#Verb|doing]] or to [[devote#Verb|devote]] oneself to some [[task#Noun|task]]; to set upon.
##: {{synonyms|en|begin upon|[[embark]] on|take in hand}}
##: {{ux|en|He '''set about''' designing his homepage.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1963|month=June|title=News and Comment: Road–rail Co-operation|journal=Modern Railways|page=362|passage=No time has been lost in '''setting about''' the implementation of non-controversial Beeching proposals.}}
##* '''22 March 2012''', Scott Tobias, AV Club ''The Hunger Games''[http://www.avclub.com/articles/the-hunger-games,71293/]
##*: But that’s a dubious triumph: A book is a book and a movie is a movie, and whenever the latter merely '''sets about''' illustrating the former, it’s a failure of adaptation, to say nothing of imagination.

